================================================================================
PROJECT CONTEXT
ENGINEERING COMPANY IT LAB
================================================================================

VERSION

    Architecture Baseline: v1.1
    Status: APPROVED
    Purpose: Master context for the entire learning project


================================================================================
PURPOSE
================================================================================

Build a realistic IT infrastructure laboratory representing
a small international engineering company.

The project is designed specifically to practice skills required
for an IT Administrator / Infrastructure / Cloud-oriented position.

The lab combines:

    IT Administration
        +
    Virtualization
        +
    Networking
        +
    Cloud
        +
    Windows / Active Directory
        +
    ITSM / Help Desk
        +
    Infrastructure as Code
        +
    Automation
        +
    Security
        +
    Troubleshooting
        +
    Documentation


The project is a HANDS-ON ADMINISTRATION LAB.

The goal is not to reproduce an enterprise environment perfectly.

The goal is to build a coherent environment where the student can:

    - administer users and computers
    - understand virtualization
    - understand networking
    - build and administer Windows infrastructure
    - practice Active Directory
    - troubleshoot incidents
    - manage permissions
    - work with ITSM workflows
    - practice AWS-style cloud concepts locally
    - use Infrastructure as Code
    - automate repetitive administrative tasks
    - understand cloud identity and permissions
    - investigate failures
    - apply security principles
    - document infrastructure and procedures
    - explain design decisions


================================================================================
IMPORTANT LEARNING PRINCIPLE
================================================================================

The student should NOT simply follow commands.

Every major component should be understood through:


    CONCEPT
        ↓
    WHY IT EXISTS
        ↓
    HOW IT WORKS
        ↓
    ALTERNATIVES
        ↓
    REAL-WORLD USE CASES
        ↓
    ARCHITECTURE
        ↓
    IMPLEMENTATION
        ↓
    FAILURE SCENARIO
        ↓
    TROUBLESHOOTING
        ↓
    DOCUMENTATION


The project should prefer realistic scenarios over isolated
technology demonstrations.


================================================================================
PROJECT FLOW
================================================================================

The project follows this high-level progression:


    LAB FOUNDATION
        ↓
    NETWORKING
        ↓
    CLOUD LAB
        ↓
    CLOUD APPLICATION
        ↓
    TERRAFORM
        ↓
    WINDOWS INFRASTRUCTURE
        ↓
    WINDOWS CLIENT
        ↓
    FILE SERVICES / PERMISSIONS
        ↓
    REMOTE IT SUPPORT
        ↓
    ITSM
        ↓
    ARCHITECTURE COMPLETION
        ↓
    TODO / FUTURE SERVICES


This order is intentional.


The project first establishes the underlying infrastructure
and cloud concepts.

Windows is introduced after the initial infrastructure
and cloud foundations are understood.

The Windows section then becomes the main
on-premises administration environment.


After the core environment is complete, the project
moves from the mandatory architecture into the
remaining TODO items.


IMPORTANT:

Not every technology in the final vision is a mandatory
core phase.

Some technologies are intentionally deferred until
there is a real architectural or learning reason
to introduce them.


================================================================================
RELATIONSHIP WITH ACQUISITIONS PROJECT
================================================================================

The student already has a separate learning project:

    ACQUISITIONS


Acquisitions focuses primarily on:

    Application
        ↓
    Node.js
        ↓
    Express
        ↓
    Docker
        ↓
    Docker Compose
        ↓
    CI/CD
        ↓
    Kubernetes
        ↓
    Observability


This project focuses primarily on:

    Infrastructure
        ↓
    Virtualization
        ↓
    Networking
        ↓
    Cloud
        ↓
    Infrastructure as Code
        ↓
    Windows
        ↓
    Active Directory
        ↓
    ITSM
        ↓
    Automation
        ↓
    Security
        ↓
    Troubleshooting
        ↓
    Documentation


The projects complement each other.

Together they create a broader practical stack:

    IT Administration
        +
    Infrastructure
        +
    Cloud
        +
    DevOps
        +
    Automation


The Acquisitions project should NOT be rebuilt inside this lab.

Concepts and tools learned there may be reused where appropriate.


