================================================================================
HOST / VIRTUALIZATION ARCHITECTURE
================================================================================

Physical environment:


HOST
│
└── Arch Linux
      │
      └── QEMU/KVM
            │
            └── libvirt
                  │
                  ├── engineering-lab network
                  │
                  ├── MINT01
                  │
                  ├── DC01
                  │
                  ├── WIN01
                  │
                  └── future VMs


Management:

    virt-manager


The host machine is NOT part of the simulated company infrastructure.

Arch Linux acts as:

    hypervisor host
    management environment
    virtualization platform


The simulated company infrastructure exists inside the VMs.


================================================================================
LIBVIRT NETWORK ARCHITECTURE
================================================================================

The primary VM network is:


    engineering-lab


Conceptual topology:


                         ARCH HOST
                             │
                          QEMU/KVM
                             │
                          libvirt
                             │
                   engineering-lab
                             │
             +---------------+---------------+
             │               │               │
             ▼               ▼               ▼
          MINT01           DC01            WIN01
             │               │               │
          Admin          AD / DNS /       Domain
        Workstation         DHCP          Client


The network is designed as a reusable internal laboratory network.

It should NOT be designed around exactly three VMs.

Future VMs may be connected to the same network without
redesigning the base topology.


================================================================================
NETWORKING DESIGN PRINCIPLE
================================================================================

The initial network should remain SIMPLE.

Initial target:


    engineering-lab
    192.168.100.0/24


Example addressing:


    MINT01
        192.168.100.10


    DC01
        192.168.100.20


    WIN01
        192.168.100.30


The exact addresses may change during implementation.

The architecture must support:


    VM-to-VM communication
    DNS
    DHCP
    routing
    firewalling
    service discovery
    troubleshooting


IMPORTANT:

Do not introduce VLANs, multiple subnets, firewall appliances,
VPNs or complex routing at the beginning.

Those are future learning topics and belong in TODO
until the architecture requires them.


