================================================================================
FILE SERVICES AND PERMISSIONS
================================================================================

The lab should eventually provide department shares.


Example:


Engineering Share
|
+-- Projects
+-- Documentation
+-- Standards
└-- Shared


Finance Share
|
+-- Documents
└-- Reports


IT Share
|
+-- Scripts
+-- Documentation
└-- Software


Access should be controlled through security groups.


Topics:


    SMB
    NTFS permissions
    Share permissions
    ACL
    inheritance
    effective permissions
    group-based access
    least privilege


A dedicated FILE01 is NOT required initially.

File Services may begin on DC01 if appropriate.

A dedicated FILE01 becomes a TODO item if the architecture
later benefits from separation of roles.


================================================================================
REMOTE IT SUPPORT
================================================================================

The lab should simulate an internal IT Help Desk.


Example incidents:


INC-001
    User cannot log in


INC-002
    User cannot access Engineering share


INC-003
    DNS resolution failure


INC-004
    DHCP problem


INC-005
    Application does not start


INC-006
    User lacks required permission


INC-007
    Windows Update failure


INC-008
    High CPU / memory usage


INC-009
    Network connectivity failure


INC-010
    Account locked


INC-011
    Software license unavailable


INC-012
    Cloud authentication / permission problem


INC-013
    Cloud application failure


INC-014
    Suspicious login / account security issue


Every incident should follow:


    SYMPTOM
        ↓
    INITIAL INVESTIGATION
        ↓
    HYPOTHESIS
        ↓
    DIAGNOSTICS
        ↓
    ROOT CAUSE
        ↓
    FIX
        ↓
    VERIFICATION
        ↓
    DOCUMENTATION


The student should learn to reason from symptoms
instead of blindly executing commands.


================================================================================
ITSM
================================================================================

ITSM is part of the CORE COMPANY ENVIRONMENT.

It is introduced after the main Windows administration
and support concepts are understood.


Technology principle:


    OPEN-SOURCE ITSM


The exact ITSM platform will be selected during
the ITSM stage based on:

    functionality
    ease of deployment
    learning value
    documentation
    licensing
    resource consumption


The project should avoid unnecessary dependence
on a proprietary ITSM platform.


Core learning scope:


ITSM
|
+-- Users
|
+-- Tickets
|    |
|    +-- Incidents
|    +-- Service Requests
|    +-- Changes
|
+-- Assets
|
+-- Software
|
+-- Licenses
|
+-- Knowledge Base
|
+-- Departments
|
└-- Audit History


Advanced ITSM functionality is deferred to TODO.


================================================================================
ENGINEERING SOFTWARE / LICENSE MANAGEMENT
================================================================================

Engineering software catalog:


    Autodesk Revit
    Bluebeam
    Revizto
    ElumTools
    SKM
    Dialux
    Tekla


The lab should model a realistic software request workflow:


    Employee
        ↓
    Software Request
        ↓
    Manager Approval
        ↓
    IT Approval
        ↓
    License Availability Check
        ↓
    License Assignment
        ↓
    Software Installation
        ↓
    Verification
        ↓
    Asset Update
        ↓
    Ticket Resolution


The workflow should also cover:


    unavailable license
    expired license
    renewal request
    license reassignment
    user leaving company
    software removal


Paid engineering software is NOT required for the core lab.


The primary learning objective is:


    software management
        +
    licensing
        +
    ITSM workflow
        +
    asset management


not learning every engineering application itself.


================================================================================
CLOUD LAB
================================================================================

Cloud environment:


    FLOCI


Purpose:


    Practice AWS-style cloud concepts locally
    without making the project dependent on
    a paid production AWS environment.


Floci is the project's primary local cloud laboratory.


The cloud section should cover, where supported and useful:


    IAM
    S3
    SQS
    Lambda
    RDS
    Secrets
    cloud networking where useful
    logging where useful


IMPORTANT:

The project is NOT a real AWS project.

The primary cloud environment is:


    FLOCI


AWS terminology may be used because the cloud model
and APIs are AWS-oriented, but the implementation
should remain local.


Do NOT create cloud services merely because they exist.

Every service must have a scenario-driven reason to exist.


================================================================================
CLOUD BUSINESS WORKFLOW
================================================================================

Primary example:


Engineering Document Workflow


Employee
    |
    v
Application / upload process
    |
    v
S3
    |
    v
SQS
    |
    v
Lambda
    |
    +-------------> process metadata
    |
    +-------------> RDS
    |
    +-------------> logging
    |
    v
Result


This scenario provides a reason to learn:


    S3
    SQS
    Lambda
    RDS
    IAM
    Secrets
    Logging


The workflow should be implemented before adding
unrelated cloud services.


================================================================================
CLOUD IAM
================================================================================

IAM should be designed around least privilege.


Example:


engineering-user

    permissions:
        limited engineering access


it-admin

    permissions:
        administrative operations


application-role

    permissions:
        application-specific operations


lambda-role

    permissions:
        S3 read
        SQS consume
        RDS access

    no:
        IAM administration


The student should intentionally create and troubleshoot
permission failures.


Topics:


    IAM Users
    IAM Groups
    IAM Roles
    IAM Policies
    Resource Policies
    Least Privilege
    Permission Evaluation
    Access Denied troubleshooting


================================================================================
SECRETS MANAGEMENT
================================================================================

Secrets should not be stored directly in:


    Git
    source code
    Terraform files
    Dockerfiles
    plain-text documentation


Conceptual flow:


Application
    |
    v
Secrets Manager / equivalent Floci mechanism
    |
    +-- database credentials
    +-- API keys
    +-- application secrets
    +-- service credentials


This should later connect with:


    Terraform
    GitHub Actions
    Lambda
    RDS


The exact implementation depends on Floci capabilities.


================================================================================
TERRAFORM
================================================================================

Terraform is the Infrastructure as Code layer.

Terraform is introduced AFTER the initial cloud
resources and architecture are understood manually.


Target architecture:


Terraform
    |
    +-- IAM
    +-- S3
    +-- SQS
    +-- Lambda
    +-- RDS
    +-- Secrets
    +-- other required infrastructure


The provider / implementation must be compatible
with the chosen Floci environment.


Learning progression:


    Terraform basics
        ↓
    Provider
        ↓
    Resources
        ↓
    Variables
        ↓
    Outputs
        ↓
    State
        ↓
    Plan
        ↓
    Apply
        ↓
    Destroy
        ↓
    Modules
        ↓
    Environment management
        ↓
    Drift


Important concepts:


    declarative configuration
    desired state
    actual state
    Terraform state
    dependency graph
    drift
    plan
    apply
    destroy
    idempotency


The student should understand WHY Terraform is useful,
not merely learn Terraform syntax.


================================================================================
AUTOMATION
================================================================================

Automation is introduced AFTER the manual administration
workflows are understood.


Primary tools:


    PowerShell
    Bash
    Python
    Terraform
    GitHub Actions


Possible automation:


    create user
    disable user
    reset account
    provision workstation configuration
    check DNS
    check service health
    collect system information
    create ITSM records
    update assets
    validate infrastructure
    deploy cloud infrastructure
    run health checks


Automation should always begin with understanding
the manual process first.


Manual Process
    ↓
Understand
    ↓
Identify repetition
    ↓
Automate
    ↓
Validate
    ↓
Document


================================================================================
GITHUB ACTIONS / CI/CD
================================================================================

GitHub Actions should automate repository and
infrastructure-related workflows.


Possible workflow:


git push
    |
    v
GitHub Actions
    |
    +-- lint
    +-- tests
    +-- Terraform fmt
    +-- Terraform validate
    +-- Terraform plan
    |
    v
deployment / approval
    |
    v
Terraform apply


CI/CD is introduced only after Terraform
and the underlying infrastructure are understood.


Security:


    GitHub Secrets
    environment protection
    least privilege
    deployment permissions


================================================================================
MONITORING / OBSERVABILITY
================================================================================

Monitoring is NOT a mandatory standalone core phase.

The project should first use native diagnostic tools:


Windows:


    Event Viewer
    Performance Monitor
    Event Logs
    Services


Linux:


    journalctl
    systemd
    top
    ps
    free
    df
    ss
    ip


Network:


    ping
    ip
    ss
    nslookup
    dig
    traceroute
    curl


Prometheus, Grafana, centralized logging
and other observability infrastructure belong to TODO.


They should be introduced only when:

    the current infrastructure needs monitoring
        OR
    a monitoring-specific learning scenario is selected.


Mental model:


    Logs
        =
    What happened?


    Metrics
        =
    How is the system behaving?


    Traces
        =
    How did a request move through the system?


================================================================================
SECURITY
================================================================================

Security is NOT a separate final phase only.

Security should be considered throughout the project.


Core principles:


    Least Privilege
    Authentication
    Authorization
    MFA where applicable
    Password Policies
    Account Lockout
    GPO Security
    Windows Firewall
    IAM Policies
    Secrets Management
    Audit Logs
    Patch Management
    Backups
    Access Reviews


Advanced security infrastructure such as:

    VPN
    network segmentation
    advanced firewalling
    centralized security tooling

is deferred to TODO until justified.


Security should be taught through practical failures.


================================================================================
INCIDENT SIMULATION
================================================================================

A major goal of the project is troubleshooting.


The environment should intentionally contain
controlled failures.


Possible scenarios:


    DNS failure
    DHCP failure
    AD authentication failure
    account lockout
    incorrect GPO
    incorrect NTFS permissions
    incorrect share permissions
    broken service
    unavailable network
    incorrect firewall rule
    expired software license
    missing software
    broken Windows update
    high resource usage
    cloud permission failure
    unavailable S3 resource
    Lambda failure
    database connectivity failure
    expired secret
    Terraform drift


Each scenario should be investigated like a real IT incident.


