================================================================================
TROUBLESHOOTING DOCUMENTATION
================================================================================

Troubleshooting is documented DURING implementation.

When a non-trivial problem occurs, it should be treated
as a real learning / incident case.

The workflow is:


    PROBLEM
        ↓
    SYMPTOM
        ↓
    INITIAL HYPOTHESIS
        ↓
    INVESTIGATION
        ↓
    DIAGNOSTICS
        ↓
    ROOT CAUSE
        ↓
    FIX
        ↓
    VERIFICATION
        ↓
    LESSON LEARNED
        ↓
    DOCUMENTATION


Examples of problems worth documenting:


    - libvirt network definition failure
    - bridge creation failure
    - DHCP failure
    - DNS failure
    - VM connectivity failure
    - permission problem
    - service startup failure
    - incorrect configuration
    - authentication failure
    - Terraform error
    - cloud permission error
    - automation failure


Not every trivial typo requires an incident document.

A troubleshooting case should be documented when
the problem provides useful knowledge about:


    architecture
    configuration
    system behavior
    diagnostics
    failure modes
    administration
    security
    or troubleshooting methodology.


The goal is not only to record the final fix.

The documentation should capture:


    WHAT happened
    WHY it happened
    HOW it was diagnosed
    HOW it was fixed
    HOW to verify the fix
    WHAT was learned


Troubleshooting cases become part of the project's
practical knowledge base and portfolio evidence.


================================================================================
LEARNING METHOD
================================================================================

Teaching style:


    1. Work through one phase at a time.
    2. Divide phases into stages.
    3. Divide difficult stages into smaller parts.
    4. Explain concepts before implementation.
    5. Connect new concepts to previously learned concepts.
    6. Discuss real-world alternatives.
    7. Discuss failure scenarios.
    8. Ask conceptual questions.
    9. Let the student answer.
    10. Discuss / correct the answer.
    11. Let the student implement.
    12. Review the implementation.
    13. Create a troubleshooting scenario.
    14. Document the result.
    15. Update progress.
    16. Continue only after understanding is confirmed.


IMPORTANT:

Do NOT simply provide finished configurations.

Prefer:


    Concept
        ↓
    Why
        ↓
    Architecture
        ↓
    Alternatives
        ↓
    Question
        ↓
    Student answer
        ↓
    Implementation
        ↓
    Failure scenario
        ↓
    Troubleshooting
        ↓
    Review
        ↓
    Documentation


The student prefers learning through reasoning and questions.


================================================================================
SCENARIO-DRIVEN LEARNING
================================================================================

The project should be driven by realistic business scenarios.


PRIMARY SCENARIO
----------------

New Engineering Employee


    Employee joins company
        ↓
    Create AD account
        ↓
    Assign groups
        ↓
    Apply GPO
        ↓
    Domain join workstation
        ↓
    Create ITSM asset
        ↓
    Request engineering software
        ↓
    Check license
        ↓
    Assign license
        ↓
    Install software
        ↓
    Give access to Engineering share
        ↓
    Verify
        ↓
    Document


SUPPORT SCENARIO
---------------

User reports a problem


    User
        ↓
    ITSM Ticket
        ↓
    Initial Investigation
        ↓
    Diagnostics
        ↓
    Root Cause
        ↓
    Fix
        ↓
    Verification
        ↓
    Ticket Resolution
        ↓
    Knowledge Base / Documentation


CLOUD SCENARIO
--------------

Engineering document workflow


    Employee
        ↓
    Application
        ↓
    S3
        ↓
    SQS
        ↓
    Lambda
        |
        +----> RDS
        |
        +----> Logs
        |
        +----> Audit information


SECURITY SCENARIO
-----------------

Suspicious account activity


    Alert
        ↓
    Investigation
        ↓
    Identify account
        ↓
    Disable / restrict access
        ↓
    Revoke credentials where applicable
        ↓
    Review permissions
        ↓
    Verify
        ↓
    Document incident


